  "coverage": [
    "Original draws atomically capture exact start/end positions under the active cursor lock. Recipes retain a private key reference and bounded metadata without retaining sampled matrices.",
    "CPU rand_chacha oracles match original generation, repeated regeneration and query rows at odd positions, high counters and the end of the 64-bit block stream. Replays do not acquire or mutate the active cursor.",
    "Concurrent active clones cannot interleave draws within a recipe batch. Concurrent replay queries have independent scratch and reproduce the same CPU results.",
    "A batch of 256 recipes succeeds within a 64 KiB managed budget while retaining no sample matrices. Recipe-state exhaustion, byte/admission limits, query geometry and host output bounds reject before consuming randomness.",
    "Native gathers preserve physical row order and duplicates for 1, 31, 32, 33 and 4096 queries, covering partial and multiple GPU blocks. Only public indices upload; queried salt words and accepted-count status download.",
    "Base, quadratic and cubic input commitments on shifts 1, 7 and 13 using replayed salts match independent CPU Poseidon2 roots and authentication paths. A metadata-only alias binds physical salt rows to the input coset without copying or transforming samples. Salt generation and replay perform no sample upload or complete-salt readback before the audit.",
    "The commitment consumer checks runtime/domain ownership and admits sampling and hashing peaks before private work. A budget that fits sampling but not hashing rejects without new GPU operations or RNG consumption.",
    "Post-batch failure, invalid status, rejection exhaustion, unwind, altered replay boundaries and downstream consumer errors retire the shared RNG family. Proof adapter failure also retires escaped replay recipes.",
    "Shared geometry and workspace planning preserve OpenCL semantics. OpenCL replay/sampler/challenger/scalar/quotient regressions, streaming allocation checks, CPU/OpenCL builds, Apple Metal cross-compilation and standalone CUDA checks pass."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Complete hiding PCS and polynomial randomization are not yet integrated into native CUDA proving. Wallet and recursive native CUDA proofs, remaining stage coverage, worker admission and pool integration are still unfinished.",
    "This correctness checkpoint does not measure complete proof speedup or transaction throughput. Default production backend, proof parameters and verifier rules are unchanged.",
    "V100 kernels compile through NVRTC for compute_70, but V100 execution remains untested. Apple Metal execution is also untested on this Linux host."
  ],
  "qualification_note": "Earlier passing runs preceded additional maximum-query coverage and a review fix binding canonical salt recipes to shifted input cosets. This evidence records the complete rerun from frozen final source, including shifted-coset CPU oracles, plus a separately bounded streaming build. Earlier runs remain in the parent artifact directory.",
